# Vendored third-party sources are stored byte for byte, so that the
# checksum recorded beside them still identifies the upstream file after a
# clone. rapidhash.h ships with CRLF line endings; normalising them would
# change its hash and quietly turn the pin in vendor/rapidhash/README.md
# into a number that matches nothing.
vendor/rapidhash/rapidhash.h -text
vendor/rapidhash/LICENSE -text
